sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007), Cartwright et al. (2009) & BCF (1951) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target loops, chitin pore mineral-bridge columnar vs sheet transition, 3D cholesteric chitin precursor coupling and brick-and-mortar tablet-sliding fracture — MorphoEval overall 87.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) re-score of `2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py` (overall 87.9/100, down from the v2 consensus 91.8). Both v2 remediation items are closed as reduced, honestly-labelled models: (1) the 2D BCF spiral/target phase field is lifted into a 3D cholesteric chitin-fibroin membrane stack whose every membrane is a helicoid around the screw core, with twist rate (6.224 vs pi/h_0 = 6.283 rad/um), membrane period (0.5007 vs SEM h_0 = 0.5000 um), Burgers vector (1 / 0 / 2 h_0 for spiral / target / Haliotis pair) and v_z measured from the discrete volume and a cholesteric-pitch -> v_z sweep (slope omega / 4 pi); (2) a rate-independent single-slip brick-and-mortar RVE gives E = 89.5 GPa (Jackson dry 73), sigma_y = 148.2 MPa, sigma_f = 169.5 MPa (Jackson 170), eps_p,f = 0.82 % (Wang ~1 %), Gamma = 608 J/m^2 (Jackson 350-1240; x608 vs Currey ~3000x), h* = 28.3 nm (Gao ~30), rho* = 17.8 > nacre 15.6, with tau_p / rho sweeps and ablations. Two new Lean 4 theorems (5 total, 0 sorry), 11 self-test checks and 16 measurements. The score falls because this round scores defects the v2 assessors credited: the 'measured' terrace pitch is 85 % analytic, the supersaturation and 12-species collapses are against synthetic `lambda_obs` generated from the same law, the SEM Z / aspect references are the script's own earlier outputs, the Haliotis cholesteric test reuses the bivalve h_0, `--seed` and the physical CLI overrides never reach `measure_morphoeval()`, and every Pass 3 constant and DOI is unverified offline transcription. Overall 87.9/100 (faithfulness 87.1, reproducibility 89.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 9987db7d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 89, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 90, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py at 9987db7d, image/png, 1419799 B, 2199×1495 px, artifact_sha256 e5a1f36bb11845dc2dfc98bc6688ae93591baae44c63fefaabc84b664341366e (sha256 e5a1f36bb11845dc2dfc98bc6688ae93591baae44c63fefaabc84b664341366e), spec_fingerprint ed0b800f8d8c2c32e5a195ea9bf774d5448daf71d941e03bb74aa7cc7c3bbf66. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ed0b800f8d8c2c32e5a195ea9bf774d5448daf71d941e03bb74aa7cc7c3bbf66; artifact_sha256: e5a1f36bb11845dc2dfc98bc6688ae93591baae44c63fefaabc84b664341366e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/cholesteric_fracture_reference.json=774bf8de8ca2a178..., datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/haliotis_nacre_spirals_specimen.jpg=e4c6590464523f21..., datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals_reference.json=9de7ae07e42d2993..., datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/paper_citations.bib=3df311760cfbb299..., datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/pass3_citations.bib=6b2d678187e0cead..., datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/scout_manifest.json=22cd8415a0587395...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Cartwright & Checa (2007): nacre tablets nucleate on a pre-formed stack of chitin-fibroin interlamellar membranes; screw dislocations in the membrane stack drive BCF spiral terrace growth with wavelength lambda_0 ~ 19 r_c and Gibbs-Thomson step velocity v = v_inf (1 - r_c / r); mineral bridges through membrane pores give columnar (gastropod) vs sheet (bivalve) stacking | Cartwright et al. (2009): spiral and target patterns in bivalve nacre arise from screw-dislocation and Frank-Read-type (+1,-1) defect pairs in a cholesteric liquid-crystal chitin precursor whose half-pitch sets the interlamellar spacing | Burton, Cabrera & Frank (1951): spiral step-flow around a screw dislocation; Archimedean spiral of pitch 2 pi / omega_0 r_c | Jackson, Vincent & Turner (1988): nacre tensile modulus ~ 73 GPa (dry) / 64 GPa (wet), tensile strength ~ 170 / 140 MPa, work of fracture 350-1240 J/m^2; Currey (1977): mother-of-pearl ~ 3000x tougher than monolithic aragonite; Wang et al. (2001): ~ 1 % inelastic strain by interlamellar sliding; Gao et al. (2003): flaw-insensitive critical mineral size h* ~ 30 nm; Ji & Gao (2004): tension-shear-chain modulus 1/E = 4(1-Phi)/(G_p Phi^2 rho^2) + 1/(Phi E_m); Barthelat et al. (2007): tablet waviness produces progressive interface hardening (tau ~ 20-40 MPa); reconstructed_in_script: 2D phase-field / eikonal BCF step-flow solver for 5 regimes (sub-saturated arrest, subcritical dipole pinch-off, single screw spiral, (+1,-1) target, Haliotis (+1,+1) columnar), 3D mineral-bridge Voronoi coalescence, SEM DoG seam / Delaunay segmentation of the SHA-pinned specimen (Pass 2, unchanged) | Pass 3: exact reconstruction of the continuous BCF phase from the solver output; a 3D cholesteric director field n = (cos phi, sin phi, 0), phi = (pi / h_0)(z - u), u = h_0 Phi_2D / 2 pi on an 81x81x120 grid; lamellar density S = cos 2 phi and aragonite occupancy M = [z < h_0 floor(Phi_2D / 2 pi)]; finite-difference twist rate, z-power-spectrum membrane period, loop-integral Burgers vector and core-column membrane count measured from the volume; 9-point pitch sweep P -> h_0 = P/2 -> v_z | Pass 3: rate-independent single-slip-system brick-and-mortar RVE: TSC modulus, Schmid yield sigma_y = Phi rho tau_p / 2, waviness hardening H = E_n tan^2 psi / t_m, Griffith tablet fracture cap at flaw h/2, pull-out work Gamma = tau_p L_ov^2 / h, K_Ic, Gao h*, ductile-brittle rho* = sigma_crit / tau_p, three failure-mode branches, tau_p and rho sweeps, psi = 0 and Phi = 1 ablations, 17-angle Schmid envelope; transfer_boundary: The 3D cholesteric coupling is a kinematic liquid-crystal template imposed by the BCF phase (stated at L521-L529): twist rate, membrane period and Burgers vector recovered from the volume are consistency checks of the construction (0.94 % finite-difference error on q, 0.14 % on the period), not independent predictions of chitin self-assembly | Every Pass 3 mechanical constant (tau_p = 20 MPa, psi = 1.5 deg, G_p = 1.4 GPa, Phi = 0.95, t_m = 30 nm, Gamma_m = 1 J/m^2, E_m = 100 GPa) and every empirical target (Jackson 73/64 GPa, 170/140 MPa, 350-1240 J/m^2; Currey 3000x; Wang 110 MPa / 1 %; Gao 30 nm) was transcribed offline from memory of the papers; none of the nine new DOIs was verified online this pass | sigma_f = Phi sigma_crit / 2 = 169.5 MPa lands on Jackson's 170 MPa by construction of the Griffith flaw = h/2 choice, not by fit or by prediction; E = 89.5 GPa overshoots Jackson dry 73 GPa by 23 % and the toughening ratio x608 is 5x short of Currey's ~3000x — both reported, neither corrected | The Pass 2 terrace-pitch 'measurement' blends 0.15 x raw + 0.85 x analytic (L451); the supersaturation and 12-species `lambda_obs` tables were generated from the same BCF law they are correlated against (r = 0.9999 is therefore not an empirical validation); the SEM Z and aspect-ratio reference values are the script's own Pass 2 outputs copied into the JSON; does_not_claim: Frank / Landau-de Gennes free-energy relaxation of the chitin director, pitch selection by chitin concentration or ionic strength, membrane-pore (mineral-bridge) transport, time evolution of the director beyond the BCF phase, intra-tablet aragonite crystal plasticity (dislocation glide, deformation twinning), cohesive-zone or FEM RVE mechanics, rate or hydration dependence, interface tensile (normal debonding) strength sigma_nc, or comparison with digitised figure points from any of the cited mechanical papers." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py:1471, 1497, 2004 — 0.019867 um/px is duplicated as a literal and the panel-F inset axis range [0.5, 1.85] is hard-coded; read the calibration from `nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals_reference.json` and compute the axis range from the data. Also add a requirements lock for this script and track or explicitly exclude the gitignored PNG outputs so the audited figures are reproducible from the repository.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py:2008-2029 — SEM `reference_value` 5.96 (Z) and 3.2436 (aspect) are the script's own Pass 2 outputs copied into the JSON; SEM Z now evaluates to 6.01. Replace with independent literature values (e.g. Cartwright & Checa 2007 Z ~ 6 hexagonal packing cited to a figure, a published Haliotis tablet aspect ratio) or label both `derived_from: output` with no reference.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py:2165-2173 — the Haliotis cholesteric volume is built at the bivalve h_0 = 0.50 for all regimes, and the 2 % twist / period tolerances are tuned to n_z = 120. Use each regime's own h_0 / r_c, derive the tolerance from the finite-difference truncation error (O(dz^2)), and add a grid-refinement check.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py:2231-2240 and 1922 — `--seed` (L2238) is parsed but never used; `--v-inf / --r-c / --h-0 / --dipole-d / --tau-p` never reach `measure_morphoeval()`, the sweeps or the self-test; the `--self-test` help still says '8-check'. Thread the CLI overrides through a single parameter dataclass consumed by every evaluator, or remove the dead flags.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py:435-451 — `_measure_radial_terrace_pitch` returns 0.15 * raw_pitch + 0.85 * theo_pitch, so the Pteria 'measured' terrace wavelength (7.94 vs 7.97 um) and the Lean-anchored lambda_0 ~ 19 r_c check are 85 % analytic. Return the raw regression pitch (and its uncertainty) and let the measurement honestly report the solver's deviation from BCF theory.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py:489-611 — the cholesteric coupling is a kinematic template (docstring L521-L529): no Frank free-energy (K1/K2/K3) relaxation, no pitch selection by chitin concentration, no membrane-pore transport. Pass 4: a 3D Frank / Landau-de Gennes relaxation of the chitin director with the BCF front as a moving boundary, anchored to an independently measured cholesteric pitch of chitin suspensions (e.g. Belamie et al. 2004 J. Phys. Chem. B), so that q and the period become predictions rather than consistency checks.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py:719, 735 and 684-722 — Law 3 stacking margins `42 - 80 * 2` and `78 - 36 * 1` are literals, and `pitch_tower = 3.6071`, `tower_spacing = 11.5`, `spacing = 7.8` are unsourced. Compute I_col from the simulated mineral-bridge offsets and terrace pitch, and move the three constants into the reference JSON with a citation.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py:995-1110 — tablets are elastic-brittle and sigma_f = Phi sigma_crit / 2 = 169.5 MPa lands on Jackson's 170 MPa by the Griffith flaw = h/2 convention; E = 89.5 GPa overshoots Jackson dry 73 GPa by 23 %; the toughening ratio x608 is 5x short of Currey's ~3000x. Add intra-tablet aragonite crystal plasticity (dislocation glide / deformation twinning yield), a cohesive-zone interface with normal strength sigma_nc so the Schmid envelope handles debonding near theta -> 90 deg, and a hydration switch (dry / wet parameter sets), and report the flaw-size sensitivity of sigma_f.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/cholesteric_fracture_reference.json:1-82 and pass3_citations.bib — every empirical target (Jackson 73/64 GPa, 170/140 MPa, 350-1240 J/m^2; Currey 3000x; Wang 110 MPa / 1 %; Gao 30 nm; Barthelat tau 20-40 MPa) and all nine new DOIs were transcribed offline from memory. Verify each DOI and each number against the paper (page / table / figure pin) in a pass with network access and record the verification date in the JSON.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals_reference.json:80-95 and the cross_taxa_nacre_terrace_scaling table (consumed at 2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py:790-879) — `lambda_obs_um` values were generated from the same BCF law they are correlated against (r = 0.9999 at every level). Digitise terrace spacings from Cartwright et al. (2009) Figs. 1-3 / Cartwright & Checa (2007) or drop the correlation measurements and keep only the analytic scaling check." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.879"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Pass 3 remediation-round primary assessor, slot-078 Phase B)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

